 ## Latest Source Checkpoint
 
+Notification API states and the header menu supersede the project catalog snapshot
+below. This is source QA, not runtime release acceptance.
+
+- Task source: `8b8f05c33ae7b1d76621dc4b7e51522ba39ef2d1`.
+- Base source: `4de2cd69894320815deeac4c5e981b1ce38270e6`.
+- Base installed/source fingerprint:
+  `5c067887d2ec9c6c400756afc27dbc31d0feefaaa8af6141480ece30c8e5daac`.
+- Product fingerprint:
+  `7236cd8438ffc358cca5c10f49dfb90c7cbe282038a8f958a85047d02fc106a1`.
+- Frozen offline installation with `--force` refreshed the file dependency;
+  lockfile and generated API schema did not change.
+
+| Command | Exit | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| `pnpm install --offline --frozen-lockfile --force` | 0 | `task-notification-menu-install.log` |
+| `pnpm test --maxWorkers=2` | 0 | `task-notifications-release-source-units.log`; 346 tests, 47 files |
+| `pnpm lint` | 0 | `task-notifications-release-source-lint.log` |
+| `pnpm build` | 0 | `task-notifications-release-source-build.log`; typecheck and Vite |
+| Installed UI gate and `--fingerprint` | 0 | `task-notifications-release-source-ui-gate.log`; 16 route patterns |
+| Chromium smoke, one worker, `--max-failures=1` | 0 | `task-notifications-release-source-browser.log`; 8 tests, 4.8 minutes |
+| README validator and Python script tests | 0 | README validation and 4 script tests; gallery provenance remains pending |
+| Scoped Prettier and `git diff --check` | 0 | reviewed source delta |
+
+Base frontend: `base-dropdown-viewport-units.log`, 96 Vitest tests (22 files),
+18 script tests and semantic contrast check; lint/typecheck and README/hub
+validators passed. Full Rust/backend release gates were not run for this checkpoint.
+
+- Notification reads and mutations retain HTTP status/body in Base ApiError;
+  empty 204 mark-read responses remain valid, and network failures are not
+  substituted with empty data. UI feedback does not expose diagnostic envelopes.
+- Header menu distinguishes loading/empty/error/403/404/partial. Cached access
+  revocation hides items/count; retryable refresh preserves readonly content.
+  Only repeatable errors offer retry; a failed source must recover before retrying
+  its write command. A capped visual count retains its actual accessible value.
+- Synchronous command locking prevents duplicate one/all writes. The menu stays
+  open for feedback; invalidation that removes its initiator restores safe focus,
+  but does not overwrite a deliberate focus move or steal Escape focus.
+- Base DropdownMenu owns the 8 px viewport inset and available-height cap.
+  The bounded preview has a named keyboard-focusable local scroll region, with
+  a stationary header/footer. It does not become a desktop full-height panel.
+- Final browser output contains 188 PNG files: the earlier 155 page/form/state
+  captures plus 30 menu captures (3 themes x 10 widths) and 3 controlled menu states.
+  Menu geometry, targets 40/44, End/ArrowUp scrolling, Escape/focus and normal
+  console/network checks passed. Axe found no violations in the menu at 1920 px
+  in gray/dark/light; this is not a whole-application accessibility claim.
+
+Final mobile/desktop menu and controlled-state captures were inspected visually.
+Artifacts: [current captures](../../../../audit-artifacts/base-standard-2026-10-01/task-notifications-release-source-browser/),
+[current browser log](../../../../audit-artifacts/base-standard-2026-10-01/task-notifications-release-source-browser.log).
+Earlier menu/compact/verified runs are superseded, including the intermediate
+scrollable-region-focusable failure fixed before this final run.
+
+All browser HTTP/OIDC is mocked. No accepted images, runtime pins, volumes,
+credentials, default refs or foreign checkouts were changed. The owned preview
+ended and port 18865 had no listener. Foreign candidate/validation containers seen
+in a read-only inventory were left untouched. All original findings remain open.
+The notifications page itself still needs Base composition, independent settings
+states, URL/hash preservation and draft protection; legacy counter typography/theme
+CSS, other routes, backend/actual-image/live SSO QA, real README provenance,
+consumer synchronization, local default integration and mirror remain required.
+
+## Project Catalog Checkpoint (Historical)
+
 Project catalog and guarded forms supersede the earlier shell/detail snapshot
 below. Earlier logs remain historical evidence, not proof for current runtime.
 
